VeridianOS: fix compiler warnings in libkscreen (DPMS helper, fake backend)

GCC reported:

- -Wmaybe-uninitialized for 'mode' in Dpms::org_kde_kwin_dpms_done()
  (src/libdpms/waylanddpmshelper.cpp). m_mode holds the uint the compositor
  sent in the mode event, cast to the protocol enum; the switch covered only
  the four known values, so any other value (a newer compositor) emitted
  modeChanged() with an uninitialized KScreen::Dpms::Mode. Small real bug:
  an unknown value is now logged with the file's KSCREEN_DPMS category and
  nothing is emitted. Known values behave as before.
- -Wdeprecated-declarations for QVariant::type(), canConvert(int) and
  convert(int) in Parser (backends/fake/parser.cpp). Ported to
  QVariant::metaType() with canConvert(QMetaType)/convert(QMetaType), which
  the deprecated overloads forward to. Same behaviour for built-in types;
  for user-registered types type() collapsed the id to QVariant::UserType,
  so the new code converts them correctly where the old code could not.
- -Wunused-result for QFile::open() in Fake::edid() (backends/fake/fake.cpp).
  A failed open fell through to parsing an empty read, which also ended in
  an empty QByteArray; it now logs the error with KSCREEN_FAKE and returns
  QByteArray() directly, as the parser's own file loading does.

diff -ru a/backends/fake/fake.cpp b/backends/fake/fake.cpp
--- a/backends/fake/fake.cpp	2026-10-08 17:06:51.791580706 -0400
+++ b/backends/fake/fake.cpp	2026-10-08 17:07:51.237792291 -0400
@@ -105,7 +105,10 @@
 {
     Q_UNUSED(outputId);
     QFile file(mConfigFile);
-    file.open(QIODevice::ReadOnly);
+    if (!file.open(QIODevice::ReadOnly)) {
+        qCWarning(KSCREEN_FAKE) << "Cannot open" << mConfigFile << file.errorString();
+        return QByteArray();
+    }
 
     const QJsonDocument jsonDoc = QJsonDocument::fromJson(file.readAll());
     const QJsonObject json = jsonDoc.object();
diff -ru a/backends/fake/parser.cpp b/backends/fake/parser.cpp
--- a/backends/fake/parser.cpp	2026-10-08 17:06:51.772552373 -0400
+++ b/backends/fake/parser.cpp	2026-10-08 17:07:49.767803357 -0400
@@ -89,8 +89,8 @@
         Q_ASSERT(property.isValid());
         if (property.isValid()) {
             QVariant value = iter.value();
-            if (value.canConvert(property.type())) {
-                value.convert(property.type());
+            if (value.canConvert(property.metaType())) {
+                value.convert(property.metaType());
                 object->setProperty(iter.key().toLatin1().constData(), value);
             } else if (QLatin1String("QVariant") == QLatin1String(property.typeName())) {
                 object->setProperty(iter.key().toLatin1().constData(), value);
